<title>FRANCE: French vote shows new EMU talks needed - Fantozzi.</title>
<headline>French vote shows new EMU talks needed - Fantozzi.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>- Italy's Foreign Trade Minister Augusto Fantozzi said on Monday that a surprise swing to the left in the first round of Frances parliamentary election should lead to further discussions of the Maastricht criteria.</p>
<p>He also said it opened the way for increased flexibility in interpreting the criteria.</p>
<p>He also told a news conference at the OECD that the left's lead, although still not a final result, pointed to a large number of countries joining a single currency in the first wave.</p>
<p>&quot;The French elections show that you have to be careful on the way to Europe,&quot; he said. &quot;It shows that additional discussions will be required in France and between other countries about the Maastricht criteria.&quot;</p>
</text>
